Recipe:&#xA0;Teriyaki Chicken Drumsticks
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
6 chicken drumsticks (thawed)&#xD;
3/4 cup balsamic vinegar&#xD;
1 teaspoon garlic powder&#xD;
1 tablespoon honey&#xD;
2 tablespoons soy sauce&#xD;
sesame seeds&#xD;
chives&#xD;
&#xD;
Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Spray a large heavy skillet with cooking spray. Heat the skillet on medium high heat and add the chicken drumsticks to the pan.&#xD;
Brown the chicken on the outside for around 10 minutes or until the skin starts to become crispy. Meanwhile, mix balsamic vinegar, soy sauce, honey and garlic in a small bowl.&#xD;
Once the chicken has browned on all sides add the mixture and reduce heat to low and cover skillet with a lid.&#xD;
Cook for at least 20 minutes or until the chicken has cooked thoroughly.&#xD;
Take lid off of the pan and turn the heat to high for around 5-8 minutes to reduce and thicken the sauce. The sauce will start to boil and become thicker and thicker.&#xD;
