Recipe:&#xA0;Brazilian Rice with Ground Beef
&#xD;
Ingredients:
&#xD;
&#xD;
1 Cup&#xA0;enriched long grain rice (uncooked)&#xD;
1 Tbsp. canola oil&#xD;
4 Tbsp. chopped yellow onion&#xD;
2 cloves garlic, minced&#xD;
1/2 tsp. salt&#xD;
2 Cups&#xA0;hot water&#xD;
about 1 or 1 1/2 Cup cooked ground beef&#xD;
about 1 pinch ground cumin&#xD;
salt and pepper to taste&#xD;
&#xD;
Instructions:
&#xD;
&#xD;
Heat a pot or pan (with tight fitting lid) to medium-high heat. Add oil.&#xD;
Add onions and cook for about 1 minute. Add garlic and cook until garlic starts turning light brown.&#xD;
Add uncooked rice and salt. Mix frequently so nothing burns. Continue cooking until rice starts turning light brown.&#xD;
Add water. Stir. Place tight fitting lid on pan/pot. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to a simmer. Let cook for about 18-20 minutes, or until the water is absorbed.&#xD;
Set aside, but keep lid on until ready to serve.&#xD;
Heat the cooked ground beef. Add cumin, salt, and pepper to taste.&#xD;
Serve rice topped with ground beef mixture. Goes great with steamed carrots!&#xD;

